  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A palace sat on top of a 180-metre rock. Sigiriya, in central Sri Lanka, built in the fifth century.",
        "visual_query": "sri lanka rock fortress aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "rock fortress"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Halfway up, the stairs pass between two giant carved lion's paws. The head that once sat above them collapsed long ago.",
        "visual_query": "sigiriya lion staircase stone paws",
        "visual_fallback": "stone staircase"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Paintings once covered 140 metres of the western cliff, and twenty-two of them survive. Who goes to this much trouble to live on a rock?",
        "visual_query": "ancient sri lankan cliff fresco",
        "visual_fallback": "cliff painting"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The chronicles give a reason. Kashyapa had seized the throne, and he feared his half-brother Moggallana would come back to take it.",
        "visual_query": "sri lankan ancient royal ruins",
        "visual_fallback": "royal ruins"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Moggallana came back in 495 and won. The capital moved away, monks took over the rock, and later visitors scratched 685 poems into its polished wall.",
        "visual_query": "sri lanka buddhist monastery ruins",
        "visual_fallback": "monastery ruins"
      }
    ],
